; Meadow — Meadow terrain visual (emits `open_grass` + `flowers`), variant 1 of 3: the flower
; CLUMP read. Still the first and only source of the `flowers` habitat tag.
;
; 24x Grass_Common_Short MultiMesh at 0.075 + 2x Flower_3_Group at 0.146 + 2x Flower_4_Group at
; 0.1206. Both flower scales are UNCHANGED from what this scene already shipped (raw AABB
; heights 2.054835 and 2.486768, both to a ~0.30 tile-unit target).
;
; WHAT CHANGED (2026-09-08 grass-family rework): the tile gained a real GRASS BASE. It
; previously carried flowers on a bare tinted slab, which left it reading as "slab with props"
; next to Grass's dense lawn even though both terrains emit `open_grass`. The base is the same
; mesh, scale and MultiMesh treatment Grass uses, so the two now share a floor and Meadow's
; flowers are the only thing that distinguishes them — which is exactly the tag difference.
;
; BUILT BY A ONE-OFF HEADLESS SCRIPT, NOT HAND-AUTHORED, AND NOT EDITABLE BY HAND — same
; generator, buffer layout and headless caveat as the four Grass variants; see
; GrassCommonShort.tscn's header for the full explanation. Re-run the generator to change
; anything below; do not hand-edit the MultiMesh buffer.
;
; INHERITS THE GRASS CALIBRATION BASELINE (human sign-off 2026-09-08): slab BoxMesh
; 1.0 x 0.2 x 1.0 at y=-0.1 (the 1.0 width is the cross-tile seam-gap fix, do not narrow it),
; blotchy floor patches at y=0.001, fixed-seed deterministic scatter within +/-0.42 tile-units
; of centre, +/-18% scale jitter and free Y-rotation, everything ground-level nested under one
; node named "Slab" (the OcclusionFader exemption convention). The human ruled on these values
; against Grass first precisely so they would not be re-proposed per terrain.
;
; HIGH-COUNT BLADES ARE A MULTIMESH; LOW-COUNT PROPS ARE INSTANCED glTF SCENES. Props here
; number 1-3 per tile, so a MultiMesh would buy nothing, and two of the flower meshes carry
; TWO surfaces with different textures, which a single embedded MultiMesh mesh cannot express
; cleanly. Referencing the raw piece directly is also what Meadow.tscn and Scrub.tscn already
; did before this pass.
;
; Source: Stylized Nature MegaKit (Standard/free), Quaternius, CC0 1.0 Universal — License.txt
; re-checked per asset-import-pipeline.md's audit gate. See
; project/attribution/sources/quaternius_stylized_nature_megakit.tres.
;
; GRASS COLOUR: TRUE GREEN BAND (2026-09-08, human-reported "the grass is very yellow").
; Grass.png is a 4-band vertical palette strip, each band 28px of a 512px texture, and the
; colour of every blade in this project comes from WHICH BAND its UVs land in — nothing tints
; anything (albedo is pure white, no vertex colours). The bands are:
;   band 1  x 0-27    rgb(177,152,0)  gold
;   band 2  x 28-55   rgb(57,149,0)   TRUE GREEN
;   band 3  x 56-83   rgb(185,87,0)   rust
;   band 4  x 84-111  rgb(103,163,0)  yellow-green
; Band 2 was the one band NOTHING in the project sampled: the Wispy meshes ship on band 1
; (gold) and the Common meshes on band 4 (yellow-green), which is why the world read warm.
; `uv1_offset` below re-centres this material's UV span in band 2, computed per mesh from its
; own measured span so every one lands with ~7px of margin on both band edges (mip bleed).
; The MESH IS UNTOUCHED — this is a material property and is reversible by deleting one line.
;
; OCCLUSIONFADER REMOVED 2026-09-08 — ANY MENTION OF IT BELOW IS HISTORY. The per-resident
; transparency fade (D-41 §4) flickered in play and was cut outright; the script, its scene node
; and its two suites are gone. The "Slab" node stays, because every terrain scene is built
; around it and removing it would restructure all 33 for no gain — but NO CODE LOOKS THAT NAME
; UP ANY MORE. It is a grouping convention now, with no behaviour attached, so nothing breaks if
; a new scene groups differently and nothing is gained by "restoring" the exemption.
